            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "How do you know if this deployment is DF-F with VT and not AALC based? Are u relying on the value of this GPIO?\n\nHow would you do the related handling in case of AALC based racks?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SueWang13",
                        "email": "Sue.Wang@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "SueWang13"
                    },
                    "message": "Check with EE, VT and AALC cannot coexist on the same machine.\n\nBelow is description of Check_VT():\n1. When VT is NOT present, RMC need to wait for RPU_READY to be Low then do power off. Otherwise, RMC need to wait 15 seconds and then do power off.\n2. When VT IS present, RMC need to wait VT feedback then do power off. Otherwise, RMC need to wait 150 seconds and then do power off."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eldin Lee",
                        "email": "eldin.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "eldin-lee"
                    },
                    "message": "Since there are no further questions on this, I\u2019ve marked the thread as resolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 28,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This does not seem like a necessary use of devmem.  This is a GPIO, right?\n\nThis sounds like something we need to add in the cable inventory under entity-manager anyhow.  Please work with Jagpal at configuring that correctly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 28,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "@jason-hsu@quantatw.com\n\nPlease help answer the other questions i mentioned on the PR.\n\nWhat Patrick is suggesting is to expose the VTs presence as Inventory items. To do that you can -\n\n1. Update the EM configs for Ventura (ventura_scm.json) to add GPIODeviceDetect for VTs.\n2. Update ventura_cable.json to add HW inventory (along with FBPNs) for VTs.\n\n\nJFYI: @patrick@stwcx.xyz VT open/close is a state and we had started some work on that last half https://gerrit.openbmc.org/q/topic:%22liquid-valve-train%22 which we will continue this half."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 28,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eldin Lee",
                        "email": "eldin.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "eldin-lee"
                    },
                    "message": "After discussing with @paligill@gmail.com, we agreed to use the proposed [gpio_util](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/81627/6/meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-ventura/plat-svc/files/gpio_util) instead of devmem until the liquid-valve-train topic is ready."
                }
            ],
